# The "you may" and its trigger. Turn 3: the Scamp attacks Bot2's Liliana of the Veil (3 -> 2) and is not asked anything: damage to a
# planeswalker is not damage to a player. Turn 5: it connects with Bot2, Bot1 declines, so it stays and nothing proliferates (Liliana
# stays at 2). Turn 6: Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills it and its dies trigger may target its own controller (any target): Bot1 20 -> 19.

[Bot1 Deck]
Cacophony Scamp
Mountain x7
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Liliana of the Veil
Lightning Bolt
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cacophony Scamp.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Liliana of the Veil.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Attack(Cacophony Scamp > Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Attack(Cacophony Scamp > Bot2)
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cacophony Scamp.Tapped = true
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Cacophony Scamp)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
[T7 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Cacophony Scamp = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
